WHEREAS, as provided in the Georgia Constitution, the Tattnall County Board of Commissioners (“BOC”) enjoys home rule powers, including police power, and land development and governmental and supplementary powers, and the power to adopt such ordinances and regulations as necessary to perform all functions of

" government in order to promote and protect the health, safety and general welfare of the citizens and general public of Tattnall County (“County”);

WHEREAS, the BOC finds that the ordered regulation of commercial and industrial development is necessary to protect the public health, safety, welfare and property values of the citizens of the County;

WHEREAS, the BOC from time to time reviews its ordinances to ensure that its laws preserve the quality of life for citizens while imposing limited and effective regulations on certain commercial and industrial development and uses that impact quality of life;

WHEREAS, the BOC intends to study the effects of solar facilities or solar farms (hereinafter collectively referred to as “solar farms”) on the public health, safety and welfare of the County’s residents and businesses;

‘WHEREAS, the BOC intends to consider revisions to its Code of Ordinances (“Code”) designed to promote and protect the public health, safety and welfare of the County’s residents and businesses, including concerns regarding entities _ establishing, developing and operating solar farms and utility scale solar farms, which commonly requires large areas of real property and the impacts of same on the County’s residents and businesses, through zoning classifications and/or regulations and standards for distance, environmental impacts and other ancillary impacts of solar farms on surrounding properties;

WHEREAS, the BOC finds that it must take immediate and responsive action to ' protect the County, and it is in the best interests of the health, safety and welfare of the citizens of the County that no applications be accepted in the unincorporated areas of the County for a period of 180 days from the effective date of this -yesolution if or where such applications relate to the establishment, construction, development and/or operation of solar. farms or those existing or under development, including any applications for special land use permits, rezonings, zonings, land disturbance permits, building permits, business licenses, or certificates of occupancy;

